From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:41:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] DC6B: the tick's budget cuts the first-person view,
 sprite uploads budgeted, rays every 4 pixels

- view_budget(): the view casts as far as what is left of the 33.3 ms tick allows
  (cost model K x distance with a 1.3 safety, never under 10 cells or over the draw
  distance; the fog keeps its scale). Flycast, the seven breach scripts (1935 ticks
  each, demo bot): ticks over 33.3 ms 105 -> 7 (graveyard 38 -> 3, cloud_nine 55 -> 1,
  cathedral 6 -> 3, factory 3, sewers 2 and underbelly 1 -> 0).
- V3D_SPR_BUDGET: 3 new sprite textures / copies per view, the rest wait a tick.
- V3D_RAY_PX 2 -> 4: visibility was 6-8 of the 13 ms of a big view.
- dcrun: the over-budget tick lines name the 3D view's time; a line for the cuts;
  mailbox g3d_cut / g3d_dist_min.
- host tests: test_tick_budget, test_sprite_budget (fail without their code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
